WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.390
From changes to the Avengers lineup to a new
Guardians of the Galaxy movie and a whole

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.440
bunch of potential new villains, here are
some of the major changes that we can expect

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.900
to see as the Marvel Cinematic Universe moves
past Endgame into Phase 4.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.960
One of the biggest question marks surrounding
the end of Phase 3 has been who will be left

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.780
standing after the story of the Infinity Stones
wraps up.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.340
While a comic book character's story can go
on basically forever, the situation is different

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.400
when those characters are played by real people.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.420
Actors have contracts, and contracts have
expiration dates.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.500
Most of the original Avengers lineup is facing
the end of their deals with Marvel as of Avengers:

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.000
Endgame.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.400
Whether it's through heroic death or well-earned
retirement, our time with some of these characters

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.360
is coming to an end.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.840
That said, the odds of losing all six original
Avengers in a single film is kinda inconceivable,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.700
especially since we know Black Widow is getting
her own movie.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.140
But it's pretty likely that we'll be saying
farewell to some familiar faces as the saga

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.680
of the Infinity Stones come to a close, and
the next era of the MCU takes off.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.660
Things used to feel so simple, and now, everything
is about to change.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.700
"We're in the endgame now."

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:10.000
Captain Marvel dominated the box office in
2019, with the flying, photon-blasting fighter

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.040
pilot raising the stakes on what the MCU's
heroes are capable of on screen.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.400
Her solo film also laid the foundation for
a seriously super-powered future.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.420
While the movie left with Carol Danvers out
in space on her own adventures, it's clear

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.760
that Danvers will be joining up with the Earth-bound
Avengers for Endgame and its aftermath.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.320
Don't just take our word for it.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.960
Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige has said that
Captain Marvel is, quote, "about to take the

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.040
lead and be at the forefront of the entire
cinematic universe."

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.050
He's also confirmed that she'll be arriving
to the series as its most powerful character

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.820
at least, for a little while.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:46.020
Much like the actors who came before her in
the series, Brie Larson has reportedly signed

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.640
a seven-picture deal with Marvel, so we can
count on seeing a lot more of the new Captain

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.440
all the way through Phase 4, and maybe even
beyond.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.100
"I like this one."

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:02.220
Infinity War and Endgame are two of the biggest
movies in cinematic history, so it makes sense

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.260
that phase 4 is kicking off with a slightly-more-grounded
story.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:09.720
Arriving just a few months after the fourth
Avengers movie is Spider-Man: Far from Home,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.260
the second full-fledged solo movie for the
webslinger in the MCU.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.480
According to producers, the film will bring
Peter back down to Earth after his experience

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.140
with the Avengers, with the high schooler
attempting a return to normal life.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.400
As Kevin Feige put it,

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.430
"He is, quote-unquote, a normal person, lives
a normal life, with a normal environment,

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.880
who, you know, got these powers, and who is
exposed to these extraordinary things."

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:35.860
While the MCU will probably ramp up to another
Thanos-sized threat eventually, it's starting

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.320
things off with a narrower scope.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.260
One of the high points of MCU Phase 3 was
the wildly successful arrival of Black Panther.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.460
Sure, he made a handful of appearances in
Captain America: Civil War, but T'Challa's

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.360
first solo film turned heads, won Oscars,
and broke records.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.290
Black Panther also came out just months before
Infinity War hit theaters, with Wakanda playing

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.460
a key role in the movie's climactic battle.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:02.020
So even though T'Challa met a temporary end
during that finale, it's not surprising that

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.160
he's been confirmed as coming back for a sequel.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.620
While no date's been set yet for Black Panther
2, odds are that Wakanda's best will show

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.720
up again pretty quickly after Endgame has...
um... ended..

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.180
From the small-scale springboard of the first
Iron Man, the MCU has become a pretty big

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.600
place, with giant personalities to match.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.680
We've already met cosmic entities like Ego
the Living Planet, the Kree Supreme Intelligence,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.420
and everyone's favorite Mad Titan.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.480
But how about more cosmic good guys?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.500
It's time to meet a new team in Phase 4: the
Eternals.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:36.580
Rumors of a film about the Eternals gained
steam in April of 2018, just in time for Infinity

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.200
War to make universe-shattering power the
new normal.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.400
While Spider-Man and Black Panther may help
keep things grounded, the Eternals are sure

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.040
to help keep a focus on the MCU's cosmic side.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.180
The arrival of the godlike characters also
has the potential to set the stage for some

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.980
staggeringly powerful heroes and villains
as the MCU proceeds.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:04:00.080
In December 2017, news broke that Disney would
be absorbing large portions of Fox in a historic,

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.099
eight-digit merger.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.020
If you're not a fan of the Disney monopoly,
that's bad news.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.520
But for Marvel Studios fans, the development
is exciting, with huge implications for the

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.680
characters we might see in the MCU.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.040
Now that Disney has officially gained access
to Fox's intellectual property, they also

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:19.799
got the film rights to several of the company's
most famous characters, including the Fantastic

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.580
Four, the Silver Surfer, Deadpool, and the
X-Men.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.060
It's something that Marvel fans have been
clamoring for for years, Kevin Feige included.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.620
"Having access to all of the characters is
something I've been dreaming about for my

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.060
almost 20 years at Marvel."

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.080
Many Marvel fans will tell you that Guardians
of the Galaxy is one of the best things to

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.620
ever happen to the MCU.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.840
But the future of the franchise was thrown
into doubt when writer-director James Gunn

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.040
was abruptly fired in mid-2018.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.470
The situation played out in the public eye,
with actors and fans venting their anger over

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.840
the firing and Disney digging in its heels.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.340
It was eventually confirmed that Gunn's script
would be used for the postponed third installment.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.480
Finally, in March 2019, Disney relented and
rehired Gunn to finish what he started.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:08.000
Even better, it was reported that the studio
never met with or considered any replacement

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.540
director.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:13.040
Now that Gunn's back in the pilot seat, the
series is officially back on track for Vol.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:13.540
3.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.340
"Hell yes."

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:17.700
"Dope."

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:23.100
Marvel's Phase 4 isn't just changing the face
of the movies it's also revamping the TV side

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.340
of the MCU story.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.500
In late 2019, Disney will be launching a new
streaming service, Disney+, which promises

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:32.340
to be a major destination for fans of Marvel
properties.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:36.870
It's been reported that the service will host
multiple limited series centering around specific

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:41.229
characters like Vision and Scarlet Witch,
Falcon and the Winter Soldier, and the seemingly

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:42.420
unkillable Loki.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.440
But don't write these off as cheap spin-offs:
all characters will be played by their actors

00:05:46.449 --> 00:05:48.920
from the films, with big budgets to match.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:53.000
The impact the shows have on the MCU is likely
to be far greater than what we've seen from

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.520
series like Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. or the
Marvel shows on Netflix.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.440
Unlike those loosely-connected series, Kevin
Feige has made it clear that the Disney+ shows

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.180
will be essential to the MCU, directly impacting
the movies in ways we haven't seen before.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.280
So if you thought you didn't need to pay for
another streaming service… think again.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.900
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.920
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
MCU films are coming soon.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.000
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
